			<div class="content" id="post-content-1851228">
									

<p>Favorite in regards to prose/believability/etc? Probably either Roget's or Scantron's.</p>
<p>Which one is the real SCP-001? In my headcanon, if there really is one, it's probably the one Gears wrote. That said, I believe there's no SCP-001, at least not ones that we read here. In my headcanon, there's no actual SCP-001; all the proposals, are in some parallel universe, canon. My headcanon has always been &quot;everything is canon&quot;, because I think SCP reports/tales aren't only a slice of time, but also a slice of space. There's no indication that this SCP exists in a completely different plane of reality as we are. All these overlaps, discrepancies, even alternative timelines where tales occur in which the Foundation does not exist or the Foundation became a cult, are in a way, &quot;canon&quot;, because they're all occurring withing different universes.</p>
<p>Heck, we might be the universe where the Foundation exists, only there's nothing to contain.</p>

